            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty of the left main coronary artery with a 5Fr catheter system.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>639-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The protected left main coronary artery (LM) is accessible to percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA), and the procedure is usually performed with large size catheter systems. This report describes a successful PTCA of a partially protected LM through a 5Fr diagnostic catheter system in a patient with previous coronary artery bypass grafting. Such an approach is time- and cost-efficient when combined with the diagnostic study.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
